# If you prefer the allow list template instead of the deny list, see community template:
# https://github.com/github/gitignore/blob/main/community/Golang/Go.AllowList.gitignore
#
# Binaries for programs and plugins
*.exe
*.exe~
*.dll
*.so
*.dylib

# Test binary, built with `go test -c`
*.test

# Code coverage profiles and other test artifacts
*.out
coverage.*
*.coverprofile
profile.cov

# Dependency directories (remove the comment below to include it)
# vendor/

# Go workspace file
go.work
go.work.sum

# env file
.env

# Editor/IDE
# .idea/
# .vscode/

# Task lists / design documentation (docs/) are tracked in version control.
# Ignore runtime-generated reports and local session traces:
#   - docs/*.html                   Runtime-generated HTML reports
#   - docs/trace.md                 Local session trace history
docs/*.html
docs/trace.md
trace.md

# Hugo documentation site (site/) build artifacts and local lock files
# site/ source (content/hugo.yaml/layouts etc.) is version-controlled
site/public/
site/public-local/
site/.hugo_build.lock
site/resources/
site/.hugo/
site/.cache/
